s:**\n- Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to limit concurrent execution to `max_concurrent` tasks\n- Uses `asyncio.wait()` instead of `gather()` to avoid cancelling pending tasks on exception\n- On `KeyboardInterrupt`, it waits for remaining tasks to complete before re-raising the exception, ensuring their cleanup code (finally blocks) still runs\n\nYou can test it like this:\n```python\nfrom run import run_tasks\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def sample_task():\n    try:\n        await asyncio.sleep(1)\n        print(\"Task done\")\n    finally:\n        print(\"Cleanup!\")\n\nasyncio.run(run_tasks([sample_task for _ in range(5)], max_concurrent=2))\n```","ttft_ms":19743,"type":"result","duration_ms":23033,"uuid":"1a793cb8-c325-4154-80c0-cff5fd14fb92","ttft_stream_ms":743,"time_to_request_ms":75,"queued_turn_count":0}
